 ## Crash hook ownership
 `lead_desk.hooks.FlagFileHooks(flag_path)` is the single shared hook for every subprocess crash. It reads a one-shot flag file (the path comes from config or the launcher, content = a point name), deletes it, prints "simulate crash" and calls `os._exit(137)`. `tests/crash_launcher.py` and `scripts/video_crash.py` contain no hook code: each only calls `lead_desk.server.main(hooks=FlagFileHooks(path))`. In-process tests use their own `Hooks` subclass that raises `SimulatedCrash`. Hook A fires only when this call created the receipt row; hook B fires only when this call committed transaction 2 (a replay never fires either).
 
+## Host and Origin gate
+Every request, on every route, passes `_gate_error` in `server.py` before the path is read. (1) `Host` is required (sent once) and its name, port ignored and lower-cased, must be `127.0.0.1`, `localhost`, `[::1]`, the bind address (not when it is a wildcard address), or a name in `Config.allowed_hosts` (`DESK_ALLOWED_HOSTS`, comma list, each name `^[a-z0-9.-]{1,253}$` or an IPv6 address in brackets). Otherwise 403 `{"error":"forbidden_host"}`. (2) An `Origin` header, if present (sent once), must equal `http://<allowed name>:<bound port>` exactly; `null` and anything else give 403 `{"error":"forbidden_origin"}`. (3) A `Sec-Fetch-Site` header, if present, must be `same-origin` or `none`, else 403 `{"error":"forbidden_origin"}`. A refused request writes nothing: no receipt, no count in `rejected_envelopes`; its body is read and dropped before the reply. Requests without `Origin` and `Sec-Fetch-Site` (n8n's server side, scripts, tests) pass on `Host` alone. A caller that reaches the desk under another name (for example n8n in Docker, which uses the host name Docker gives the computer, host.docker.internal) sets `DESK_BIND` to the address the desk must listen on and `DESK_ALLOWED_HOSTS` to that name.
+
+## Portal routes
+Read-only pages for a person: `GET /ui` answers 308 to `/ui/`; `GET /ui/<file>` serves one of the `.html`, `.css`, `.js` files found under `src/lead_desk/portal/` when the server started (a fixed map, never a path read from the request; anything else is 404); `/ui/demo/<file>` serves a file of the demo extension when one is installed, else 404. `GET /api/ui/summary`, `/api/ui/leads`, `/api/ui/leads/<lead_id>` and `/api/ui/review` answer JSON built from ONE read transaction on a separate read-only connection (`mode=ro`, `PRAGMA query_only=ON`): a write through it fails. Any other method on these routes is 405. `/api/demo/<rest>` goes to the demo extension (any method; 404 when none is installed; a POST body must be `application/json`, else 400 `{"error":"bad_body"}`, and at most `DEMO_BODY_MAX` bytes are handed on). Every reply, JSON or file, carries `Content-Security-Policy` (no inline script or style, no `data:`), `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`, `Referrer-Policy: no-referrer`, `Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin` and `Cache-Control: no-store`.
+
 ## Further rules
 * `Config.replies_path` defaults to `None` ("the loader supplies its own default"): `load_demo_adapters` then uses the `replies.json` that sits next to the demo folder's package, found from the package file, not from the working directory. `DESK_REPLIES_PATH` still sets it. `loader.py` is the only product module that names the demo folder (a test enforces it).
 * A submission with no email (a phone-only lead) has no lead key: verdict `review`, reason `incomplete:email` (or `incomplete:name,email` when the name is also missing); it is never merged and never dropped.
